  "body": "Found while reproducing #1091 (and the reason the #1077 reviewer's probe got a second, unrelated refusal).\n\n**What happens.** Import a casting, set the stock to \"from model\" with that casting as its source, import the part, and machine it. The casting stays in the tree as a model, and `stock_sim::part_facets_as_modelled` reads every non-fixture model as the part. So the program verdict judges the casting as finished geometry, and any cut into it - every cut, since the casting is the stock - is a gouge: `post blocked - gouge: program cuts below the model in 812 cell(s), worst 20.00 mm at (-1.75, -7.75, z 10.00)` (a Bore of a 16 mm hole in a part under a stepped casting, fixture of `crates/app/tests/stepped_stock_rapid.rs` without its `DeleteEntity` of the casting).\n\n**Expected.** A model that is only the source of a `FromModel` stock is stock, not part: the verdict (and the field view) should not read it as finished geometry. (Possibly: a model that is the source of the stock and is not the source of any operation.)\n\n**Workaround in the #1091 tests.** Delete the casting after `SetStock` - the stock keeps its own copy of the facets.\n\nDone means: a casting used as from-model stock and left in the tree posts a legal program over a separate part, pinned by a test; a model that is both the stock source and an op's source (`edge_break_gate.rs`'s brick) keeps today's verdict.\n",
